# =============================================================================
# COMINORSA Landing — Environment Variables Reference
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development overrides. The
# Cloudflare Worker bindings (ASSETS, DB, IMAGES) are NOT environment
# variables — they live in `wrangler.json` / Cloudflare dashboard.
# =============================================================================

# --- Build / Dev (optional) ---------------------------------------------------

# Set to "seatbelt" if running on macOS under Codex Seatbelt sandbox
# (forces Vite HMR polling instead of FSEvents).
# CODEX_SANDBOX=seatbelt

# Local Wrangler / Miniflare paths. The defaults below are correct for
# most environments; uncomment to override.
# WRANGLER_WRITE_LOGS=false
# WRANGLER_LOG_PATH=.wrangler/logs
# MINIFLARE_REGISTRY_PATH=.wrangler/registry

# --- Cloudflare bindings (see .openai/hosting.json) ----------------------------

# cominorsa-web is a pure SSR Worker with no persistent storage. The contact
# form posts to WhatsApp (wa.me/51987817100) and stores nothing on our side.
# Therefore `.openai/hosting.json` must NOT declare `d1` or `r2` keys -- if
# either key is present, `vinext build` injects matching `d1_databases` /
# `r2_buckets` bindings into `dist/server/wrangler.json`, and `wrangler deploy`
# will fail with code 10042 ("Please enable R2 through the Cloudflare Dashboard")
# because the bucket does not exist in this account.

# If you ever add D1 / R2 bindings in the future, edit `.openai/hosting.json`
# directly and provision the resources in the Cloudflare dashboard before
# deploying. The validator (`pnpm run validate`) will fail loudly until you do.

# --- Runtime secrets (set via `wrangler secret put`, NOT in this file) --------

# If you later add a third-party integration (SendGrid, analytics, etc.),
# store the keys as Wrangler secrets. Never commit them to the repo.
#   pnpm exec wrangler secret put SENDGRID_API_KEY
# In code, read them via env.SENDGRID_API_KEY in the Worker.

# --- Form / contact numbers (currently hardcoded) -----------------------------

# These are intentionally hardcoded in `app/ConsultationForm.tsx` and
# `app/page.tsx`. The page is one-route static; no env resolution needed.
# If the client changes their WhatsApp number, edit those two files:
#   - app/ConsultationForm.tsx  (PRIMARY_WHATSAPP)
#   - app/page.tsx              (tel: and wa.me links)
